# SABOTAGE: rule 2 of the co-adoption table — the ADR-038 §5.1 / ADR-044 §4.4a raw-bytes seam.
# The seam leg of the scan is short-circuited to `true`, so no app can ever be reported as
# mounting a signature-verifying receiver (`samen_webhook_routes/1`, `samen_fleet_routes/1`,
# `samen_fleet_ingest_routes/1`) while lacking the endpoint's `Plug.Parsers` raw-body reader. That
# half-adoption is precisely what the rule exists to catch: the macros' own @docs say the endpoint
# MUST cache the exact bytes (the ingest's says it "Needs the SAME raw-body reader"), and a host
# that skips it compiles, boots, and refuses correctly-signed deliveries as if forged —
# indistinguishable from a vendor problem, with nothing red anywhere.
# Rule 1 (the fleet cockpit pair) and every other check in the task stay intact, so the rule-2
# RED tests, their anti-tautology twins, and the GREEN real-tree discriminator assertion flip while
# the rest of the suite stays green.
# RE-ANCHORED (rule audit): the walker now reads+parses each shipped file ONCE and hands every
# signal a `sources` list (`%{path, text, ast}`) rather than a file list, which moved this hunk's
# CONTEXT lines from `files` to `sources` (and to a slightly different line number). The defect
# (the seam leg short-circuited to `true`), the added line and the MUST_FAIL target are
# byte-identical to the original.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/verify_fleet_wire_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RED (rule 2): a wire-mounting app with no raw-bytes seam is a violation
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/mix/tasks/samen.verify.fleet_wire.ex b/samen_core/lib/mix/tasks/samen.verify.fleet_wire.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/mix/tasks/samen.verify.fleet_wire.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/mix/tasks/samen.verify.fleet_wire.ex
@@ -694,7 +694,7 @@
           &wire_side_call?/1
         ),
       cockpit: Enum.any?(sources, &mounts_cockpit?/1),
-      seam: Enum.any?(sources, &wires_raw_body_reader?/1),
+      seam: true or Enum.any?(sources, &wires_raw_body_reader?/1),
       org_session:
         mount_locations(sources, [@files_macro, @csv_macro, @ics_macro], &org_session_call?/1),
       session_plug: mount_locations(sources, [], &fetch_session_plug?/1),
